    body: "# **SOP: Adding Leads from Mojo to Brivity CRM**\n\n**Owner:** Carlos (Assistant)\n\n**Frequency:** Daily, end of dialing day\n\n**Time per lead:** ~2 min\n\n**Last updated:** August 4, 2026\n\n**Purpose:** Every lead worked in Mojo gets entered into Brivity CRM the same day, with complete contact info, correct tagging, and a follow-up task set. No lead sits in Mojo only.\n\n## **Part 1 — Pull the Lead from Mojo**\n\n### **Step 1: Open Mojo and go to Home**\n\nLog into Mojo. Click **Home**.\n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n\n### **Step 2: Click \"All Agents\"**\n\nFrom the Home screen, click **All Agents**.\n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n\n### **Step 3: Select the agent whose calls you're reviewing**\n\nClick the agent name. Example: **Marco Puga**.\n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n\n### **Step 4: Set the date range**\n\nSet the date range to **Today** (or the day being worked) and hit Apply.\n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n\n### **Step 5: Open the lead**\n\nClick the lead record to open the full detail view.\n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n\n### **Step 6: Copy the following fields**\n\nCopy **all** of these out of Mojo:\n\n  - First name\n  - Last name\n  - Phone number(s)\n  - Email\n  - Property address\n  - Notes / call disposition\n\n*If a field is blank in Mojo, leave it blank in Brivity. Do not guess.*\n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n\n## **Part 2 — Enter the Lead into Brivity CRM**\n\n### **Step 7: Go to Brivity → Leads**\n\nOpen Brivity CRM. Click **Leads** in the main nav.\n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n\n### **Step 8: Click \"Add Lead\"**\n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n\n### **Step 9: Fill out the lead form**\n\n|  |  |\n| :-: | :-: |\n| **Field** | **What to enter** |\n| First Name | From Mojo |\n| Last Name | From Mojo |\n| Source | **Mojo** or **Mojo FL** — depending on which list it came from |\n| Stage | Per current call outcome |\n| Intent | **Seller** (Mojo only dials sellers) |\n| Phone | All numbers from Mojo |\n| Email | From Mojo |\n| Address | Property address from Mojo |\n| Tag | Apply the matching tag |\n\n  \n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n\n### **Step 10: Paste the notes**\n\nPaste the Mojo call notes into the description field, verbatim. Do not summarize.\n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n\n### **Step 11: Save**\n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n\n## **Part 3 — Set the Follow-Up Task**\n\n### **Step 12: Read the notes and create the task**\n\nWhatever the note says to do, set it as a task with a due date.\n\n  - Note says \"send a text in 2 weeks\" → task: *Send text*, due 2 weeks out\n  - Note says \"call back Friday\" → task: *Call back*, due Friday\n  - Note says \"not interested\" → no task, set stage accordingly\n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n\n### **Step 13: Confirm**\n\nThe lead is complete when it has:\n\n  - Full name\n  - Source + Stage + Intent\n  - Phone, email, address\n  - Tag\n  - Notes pasted\n  - Follow-up task with a due date (unless dead)\n\n## **Rules**\n\n1.  Same-day entry. No batching leads across multiple days.\n2.  Never leave Intent blank — Mojo = Seller, always.\n3.  Never skip the task. A lead with no next action is a dead lead.\n4.  Duplicates: search the name/phone in Brivity before adding. If it exists, update the existing record instead of creating a second one.",
