    body: "# SOP: After a Listing Appointment Is Set\n\n**Owner:** Carlos (Assistant) **Backup:** Wesley **Platform(s):** Brivity CRM, Google Calendar **Frequency:** On trigger — every listing appointment **Runtime:** ~10 min for logging; CMA and strategy run separately **Scope:** TX and FL **Version:** 1.0 **Last updated:** August 19, 2026\n\n  \n\n**Purpose:** Every listing appointment is logged in the CRM, on the agent's calendar with reminders, and backed by a completed CMA and listing strategy before the agent walks in. No appointment happens without preparation in hand.\n\n  \n\nThis SOP is the trigger for two others. It is not finished until both have run.\n\n## Contents\n\n1.  When to run this\n2.  Log the appointment in Brivity\n3.  Create the calendar event\n4.  Trigger the CMA\n5.  Trigger the listing strategy\n6.  Confirm before the appointment\n7.  Completion checklist\n8.  Rules\n9.  Automation opportunities\n10. Escalation\n11. Change log\n\n  \n\n## Part 01 — When To Run This\n\n**Trigger:** The agent confirms a listing appointment is set.\n\n  \n\n**Do not start before:** You have the date, time, property address, and seller name from the agent.\n\n  \n\n**Do not proceed until:** All five parts are done. Logging the appointment is 10 minutes of the work; the CMA and strategy are the rest, and they're what the appointment actually depends on.\n\n  \n\n## Part 02 — Log The Appointment In Brivity\n\n### Step 1 — Open the seller's profile\n\nConfirm **Intent: Seller** on the record.\n\n### Step 2 — Click + ADD on the Appointments panel\n\nRight sidebar.\n\n  \n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n|  |\n\n### Step 3 — Fill out the appointment form\n\n|  |  |\n| :-: | :-: |\n| **Field** | **What to enter** |\n| Task Details | **Appointment** (max 255 characters) |\n| Appointment Type | **Listing Consultation** |\n| Assigned To | The agent taking it |\n| Location | Full property address |\n| Add to Google Calendar | **Leave OFF** — see below |\n| Date | Quick option, or **Custom** for a specific date |\n| Time | Quick option, or **Custom** for a specific time |\n| Priority | **1** — listing appointments are highest priority |\n\n  \n\n**Do not.** Leave the **Add to Google Calendar** toggle off. The calendar event gets created manually in Part 03 with the correct time and reminders. The toggle produces an event you then have to fix.\n\n  \n\n**Verification checkpoint.** The quick Date and Time buttons are approximations — **Tomorrow** and **Morning 8 am**. Unless the appointment genuinely falls on one of those, use **Custom** for both. A logged time that doesn't match the real appointment is worse than no log.\n\n### Step 4 — Click SAVE\n\nLeave **Mark As Complete** unchecked.\n\n  \n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n|  |\n\n  \n\n## Part 03 — Create The Calendar Event\n\n### Step 5 — Open Google Calendar\n\n### Step 6 — Create the event\n\n|  |  |\n| :-: | :-: |\n| **Field** | **What to enter** |\n| Title | **Listing Consultation: \\[Seller Full Name\\]** |\n| Date | Actual appointment date |\n| Time | Actual start and end — block realistic duration, not a placeholder |\n| Guests | Seller's email address |\n| Location | Full property address |\n| Calendar | The agent's calendar |\n| Availability | **Busy** |\n| Notification 1 | **1 hour before** |\n| Notification 2 | **3 hours before** |\n\n  \n\n**Verification checkpoint.** Both reminders, every time. The 3-hour reminder is the one that gives the agent time to review the strategy document before driving out.\n\n  \n\n**Open item.** No standard appointment duration is set. The reference example blocks 45 minutes. A listing consultation with a walkthrough usually runs longer. Set the standard so travel time isn't eaten by an under-blocked calendar. **Owner: Marco. Due: Aug 25, 2026.**\n\n  \n\n*(screenshot — see the source document)*\n\n|  |\n\n### Step 7 — Save\n\n## Part 04 — Trigger The CMA\n\n### Step 8 — Build the CMA\n\nRun *SOP: Creating a CMA in MLS* on the subject property.\n\n  \n\nReference: <https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EeYk91J5r5Z_g56Pahmg9LIBEe8_5n5z8E0N5gj8kAk/edit?usp=sharing>\n\n  \n\n**Do not.** No appointment proceeds without a CMA. Pricing from memory in front of a seller is how a listing sits on the market for months.\n\n  \n\n## Part 05 — Trigger The Listing Strategy\n\n### Step 9 — Build the listing strategy\n\nRun *SOP: Creating a Listing Strategy* using the CMA from Step 8.\n\n  \n\nReference: <https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zIIDuitSlcJdk9D7JafnWMEl4ffdw7MCazkGsTEsDI4/edit?usp=sharing>\n\n### Step 10 — Get agent approval on the pricing\n\nPer that SOP — the agent confirms the three options before anything reaches the seller.\n\n  \n\n## Part 06 — Confirm Before The Appointment\n\n### Step 11 — Deliver the strategy to the agent\n\nNo later than 24 hours before. The agent needs time to read it, not to skim it in the car.\n\n### Step 12 — Confirm the appointment with the seller\n\nText or call the day before. Confirm date, time, and address.\n\n  \n\n**Open item.** No confirmation script exists. Draft one, or these confirmations get worded differently every time. **Owner: Carlos. Due: Aug 25, 2026.**\n\n### Step 13 — Set the post-appointment follow-up task\n\nTask for the agent, due the day after: *Follow up — listing appointment outcome*. An appointment with no logged outcome is a listing you never find out you lost.\n\n  \n\n## Part 07 — Completion Checklist\n\nA listing appointment is fully prepared when it has:\n\n  \n\n  - Brivity appointment logged — type **Listing Consultation**, correct agent, address, priority 1\n  - Custom date and time used where the quick options don't match\n  - Add to Google Calendar toggle left off\n  - Calendar event created with correct title, real start and end times\n  - Seller invited, address in the location field\n  - Both reminders set — 1 hour and 3 hours\n  - CMA built and comps vetted\n  - Listing strategy built off that CMA\n  - Agent approved the pricing\n  - Strategy delivered at least 24 hours before\n  - Appointment confirmed with the seller\n  - Post-appointment follow-up task set\n\n  \n\n## Part 08 — Rules\n\n1.  **Never toggle Add to Google Calendar.** Build the event manually.\n2.  **Use Custom date and time unless a quick option is genuinely correct.**\n3.  **Both reminders, every time.**\n4.  **Priority 1.** Listing appointments outrank everything else on the task list.\n5.  **No appointment without a CMA and a strategy.** No exceptions, including for referrals and friends.\n6.  **Strategy delivered 24 hours ahead minimum.**\n7.  **Confirm with the seller the day before.**\n8.  **Log the outcome.** Won, lost, or postponed.",
